---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, buildBreadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Cookie Policy | PictoJXL';
const description =
  'How PictoJXL and partners use cookies on pictojxl.com, what they are for, and how to control them in major browsers.';

const jsonLd = [
  buildBreadcrumbLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Cookie Policy', path: '/cookie-policy' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/cookie-policy" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <LegalPage
    title="Cookie Policy"
    description="Cookies and similar storage on pictojxl.com—what they do and how you can limit them."
    updated="October 27, 2026"
  >
    <p>
      This Cookie Policy covers how <strong>Webwise Private Company Ltd</strong> (“we,” “us”) and
      certain partners use cookies and similar technologies on
      <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>pictojxl.com</a> (PictoJXL). Read it with the
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Quick definition</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small text file a site stores on your device. Related technologies (local storage,
      pixels, and similar) can play a comparable role: remembering preferences, securing sessions,
      measuring traffic, or—when allowed—supporting advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Categories we may use</h2>
    <h3>Necessary / functional</h3>
    <p>
      These help the studio load, stay secure, and remember harmless UI choices (for example default
      slider preferences) so the tool behaves consistently across visits.
    </p>
    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>
      If AdSense or similar partners are active, advertising cookies may control delivery, frequency
      capping, and measurement. Partners may use browsing history across sites to personalize ads.
      Opt out of personalized Google ads at
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
        >Google Ads Settings</a
      >.
    </p>
    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      Analytics cookies or identifiers, when enabled, help us see aggregate traffic, popular routes,
      and technical health so we can improve PictoJXL.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Conversion is not cookie-driven upload</h2>
    <p>
      Encoding on PictoJXL runs locally with WebAssembly. Cookies are not a mechanism for uploading
      or parking your image files on our servers—those files are not sent to us for conversion in the
      first place.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Browser controls</h2>
    <p>Clear or block cookies in your browser. Paths differ by product:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies and other site data
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Safari:</strong> Settings / Preferences → Privacy → Manage Website Data / Cookies
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Firefox:</strong> Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Cookies and Site Data
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Cookies and site permissions → Manage and delete cookies
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Blocking every cookie can break preference memory and some advertising experiences.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Revisions</h2>
    <p>
      We may refresh this policy. The “Last updated” date shows the current revision.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Webwise Private Company Ltd<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
